    "Data the system has moved out to disk because RAM filled up. It is distinct from compression. A flat line at zero is ideal; a sustained climb under pressure is the real warning sign." : {
      "comment" : "Metric Cards & Explanations",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Data the system has moved out to disk because RAM filled up. It is distinct from compression. A flat line at zero is ideal; a sustained climb under pressure is the real warning sign."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "因为 RAM 装满而由系统移到磁盘的数据。它与压缩有所不同。零位置的水平线是理想状态；压力下的持续上升才是真正的危险信号。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
